---
import '../styles/site.css';
import deployment from '../../../../docs/deployments/testnet.json';

const repo = 'https://github.com/Sorogate/sorogate';
// Where the page is published (see astro.config.mjs). Astro gives the base without a trailing slash here.
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const site = 'https://sorogate.github.io';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
    <title>Sorogate policy playground</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Work out an access policy for Stellar in your browser and compare it with the answers the Soroban contract’s tests require."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={`${base}/favicon.svg`} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Sorogate policy playground" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Reusable access policies for Stellar, on Soroban. Early, Testnet only, not audited." />
    <meta property="og:url" content={`${site}${base}/`} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={`${site}${base}/og.png`} />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1280" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="640" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="A policy of three conditions worked out in order: it stops at the second and answers Denied with the reason BelowMinimum." />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#app">Skip to the playground</a>

    <header class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <nav class="topbar" aria-label="Project">
          <a class="brand" href={repo}>
            <img src={`${base}/favicon.svg`} alt="" width="32" height="32" />
            <span>Sorogate</span>
          </a>
          <span class="links">
            <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/README.md`}>Documentation</a>
            <a href={repo}>GitHub</a>
          </span>
        </nav>

        <div class="hero-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="status">
              Early development. Testnet only. Not audited. This page makes no network calls and holds no keys.
            </p>
            <h1>Sorogate policy playground</h1>
            <p class="lead">
              An access policy is a short list of conditions about an address: it holds at least some of a token, it
              holds at least some items of a collection, the ledger time is inside a window. All of them must hold.
            </p>
            <p class="lead-small">
              This page works a policy out in your browser with the project’s TypeScript model and sets the result
              beside the answer the Soroban contract’s tests require for the same input.
            </p>
            <p class="cta">
              <a class="btn primary" href="#app">Try a policy</a>
              <a class="btn ghost" href={repo}>Read the source</a>
            </p>
          </div>

          <figure class="illustration">
            <div
              class="ill-card"
              role="img"
              aria-label="Illustration: a policy of three conditions is worked out in order. The first holds, the second fails, the third is not reached, and the answer is Denied with the reason BelowMinimum."
            >
              <div class="ill-head">evaluate(policy, address)</div>
              <ol class="ill-rows">
                <li class="ill-row" style="--i: 0">
                  <span class="icon ok">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 8.5l3.2 3.2L13 4.8"></path></svg>
                  </span>
                  Holds at least 100 of a token
                </li>
                <li class="ill-row" style="--i: 1">
                  <span class="icon no">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M4 4l8 8M12 4l-8 8"></path></svg>
                  </span>
                  Holds at least 1 of a collection
                </li>
                <li class="ill-row skipped" style="--i: 2">
                  <span class="icon na"></span>
                  <span>
                    The ledger time is inside a window
                    <small>Not reached: it stops at the first failure</small>
                  </span>
                </li>
              </ol>
              <div class="ill-result" style="--i: 3">Denied: BelowMinimum, condition 2</div>
            </div>
            <figcaption>An illustration of how a policy is worked out, not a recorded run.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="wrap">
      <div id="app">
        <noscript><p class="notice">This page needs JavaScript to work a policy out.</p></noscript>
      </div>

      <section aria-labelledby="deployment-heading">
        <h2 id="deployment-heading">The public Testnet deployment</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>This is a development deployment on Stellar Testnet, not a production deployment.</strong> Testnet is
          reset from time to time, the contract has not been audited, and it has no administrator or upgrade path.
        </p>
        <dl class="facts">
          <dt>Contract</dt>
          <dd><a href={deployment.explorer}><code>{deployment.contract.id}</code></a></dd>
          <dt>WASM hash</dt>
          <dd><code>{deployment.wasm.sha256}</code></dd>
          <dt>Deployed</dt>
          <dd>{deployment.deployedAt.slice(0, 10)}</dd>
        </dl>
        <p>
          How to check that it is the code in this repository, and how it is kept alive:
          <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`}>deployment notes</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="limits-heading">
        <h2 id="limits-heading">What this page cannot tell you</h2>
        <ul class="cards">
          <li>
            <strong>The contract decides, not this page.</strong> The model here is a preview and an explanation. It is
            held to the contract by shared test vectors, but only the contract’s own answer counts on the network.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Contract answers are fixed for the listed examples only.</strong> Change a value and the page says there
            is no contract answer fixed for that input.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>A policy does not prove who is asking.</strong> The same balance passes for whoever holds it, so a
            contract that acts on a decision must also check that the caller really is that address.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Read the <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/spec/SPEC.md`}>specification</a>, the
          <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/THREAT_MODEL.md`}>threat model</a>, or the <a href={repo}>source</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="wrap">
      <p>
        Apache-2.0. Not affiliated with or endorsed by the Stellar Development Foundation; “Stellar” and “Soroban” are
        their trademarks. Set in Inter, under the <a href={`${base}/inter-OFL.txt`}>SIL Open Font License 1.1</a>.
      </p>
    </footer>

    <script>
      import { examples } from '../playground/examples';
      import { mount } from '../playground/view';

      const app = document.getElementById('app');
      if (app !== null) mount(app, examples);
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
